{{also|kuken}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|de|Kücken}} {{q|Austria, alongside ''Küken''}}

===Etymology===
Via {{der|de|nds-de|-}} from {{der|de|gml|kuken}}, from {{der|de|osx|*kiukīn}}, from {{der|de|gmw-pro|*kiukīn|t=chicken}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|kuiken}}, {{cog|en|chicken}}. A related form is {{cog|gmh|kuchil}}, whence now obsolete {{m|de|Küchlein}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈkyːkən/|[ˈkyːkən]|[ˈkyːkŋ̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Küken.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n||Küken}}

# [[chick]] {{gloss|young bird}}, [[fledgling]], [[hatchling]], [[squab]] (of a [[pigeon]] or [[dove]]))
# {{lb|de|figuratively}} the [[youngest]] in a group
# [[plug]] (as in a [[cask]])

